.
 Uncovering the unemployment rate helps clarify the non-monotonic behavior of the Gini coefficient:
 for unrealistically high unemployment,
 inequality decreases as 
\begin_inset Formula $R$
\end_inset

 increases;
 as the unemployment rate approaches more realistic levels,
